  {
   "beat_id": "B01",
   "act": "CAN-VS-SHOULD",
   "narration_text": "The wrong question is can Cowork do this. The right question is should Cowork do this. Capability and authorization are not the same. A task that Cowork is technically capable of may be one where: the data exposure is itself the problem, the judgment required is professional not clerical, the consequences are irreversible, or the institutional obligation exists regardless of AI trustworthiness. Capability does not answer any of those questions.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "remotion": {
     "pattern": "CoworkTaskView",
     "props": {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "type": "prompt",
        "text": "The wrong question is can Cowork do this. The right question is should Cowork do this. Capability an\u2026"
       },
       {
        "type": "review",
        "items": [
         {
          "title": "The wrong question is can Cowork do this.",
          "badge": "Warning",
          "badgeTone": "warn"
         },
         {
          "title": "The right question is should Cowork do this.",
          "badge": "Rule",
          "badgeTone": "pass"
         },
         {
          "title": "Capability and authorization are not the same.",
          "badge": "Warning",
          "badgeTone": "warn"
         },
         {
          "title": "A task that Cowork is technically capable of may be one where: the data exposure is itself",
          "badge": "Warning",
          "badgeTone": "warn"
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "cues": [
       0,
       18
      ]
     },
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B01.mp4",
      "at": ""
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Can vs. should \u2014 capability \u2260 authorization / data exposure / professional judgment / irreversibility / obligation",
   "spark_line": "Capability is not authorization.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 10,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 22.81,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE"
   },
   "lane": "BOOKEND",
   "voice": "am_onyx",
   "engine": "kokoro",
   "voice_kokoro": "am_onyx"
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B02",
   "act": "SEVEN-CATEGORIES",
   "narration_text": "Seven categories that belong on the nondelegation checklist. Student educational records under FERPA. Health, legal, or financial data about identifiable individuals. Risk categorization of specific people \u2014 professional judgment, not clerical work. Irreversible external actions: send, submit, delete, publish. Credentials, authentication tokens, access keys. Decisions that affect employment, academic standing, or legal status. And any action where the data exposure is itself the harm, regardless of output quality.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "callout-reveal",
    "media": "media/B02.mp4",
    "manim": {
     "scene_class": "Scene_B02_ClaudeLiamNondelegation",
     "scenes_file": "scenes_std.py",
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B02.mp4",
      "at": "2026-07-25T10:40:30.709148"
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Seven categories \u2014 FERPA / health-legal-financial / risk categorization / irreversible / credentials / status decisions / exposure harm",
   "spark_line": "Seven stops. Hard stops.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 13,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 29.44,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE",
    "src": null,
    "filled_by": null,
    "at": "2026-07-16T06:50:29",
    "needs": "PIPELINE \u2192 fill_slates/remotion_scenes for B02"
   }
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B03",
   "act": "REDESIGN-MOVES",
   "narration_text": "Three redesign moves that preserve the value while removing the problem. Reduce the data: use synthetic or anonymized examples instead of identifiable records \u2014 Cowork helps you think through the categorization criteria without seeing the real files. Reduce the action: Cowork drafts a prioritization framework, you apply it to the real files manually. Reduce the scope: Cowork processes only the aggregate data, not the individual-level records.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "callout-reveal",
    "media": "media/B03.mp4",
    "manim": {
     "scene_class": "Scene_B03_ClaudeLiamNondelegation",
     "scenes_file": "scenes_std.py",
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B03.mp4",
      "at": "2026-07-25T10:40:34.301044"
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Redesign moves \u2014 reduce data: anonymized / reduce action: draft then human executes / reduce scope: aggregate not individual",
   "spark_line": "Redesign before you delegate.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 13,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 23.02,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE",
    "src": null,
    "filled_by": null,
    "at": "2026-07-16T06:50:29",
    "needs": "PIPELINE \u2192 fill_slates/remotion_scenes for B03"
   }
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B04",
   "act": "VERDICT",
   "narration_text": "The nondelegation checklist is not a limit on what Cowork can do. It is a list of questions to answer before you decide. Human review at the end does not fix a data exposure that happened at the start. The moment identifiable records enter the session, the exposure has occurred. The checklist belongs before the task brief \u2014 run it before you open the folder.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "stagger",
    "remotion": {
     "pattern": "CoworkTaskView",
     "props": {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "type": "prompt",
        "text": "Should Cowork do this? (Not: can it do this?)"
       },
       {
        "type": "review",
        "items": [
         {
          "title": "Human review at the end does NOT fix exposure at the start",
          "badge": "Rule",
          "badgeTone": "fail"
         },
         {
          "title": "Identifiable records in session = exposure occurred",
          "badge": "Rule",
          "badgeTone": "fail"
         },
         {
          "title": "Run checklist BEFORE opening the folder",
          "badge": "Order",
          "badgeTone": "warn"
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "cues": [
       0,
       18,
       34
      ]
     },
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B04.mp4",
      "at": ""
     }
    }
   },
